&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Verve has created a more efficient and privacy-focused way to buy and monetize advertising. Verve is an ecosystem of demand and supply technologies fusing data, media, and technology together to deliver results and growth to both advertisers and publishers–no matter the screen or location, no matter who, what, or where a customer is. With 30 offices across the globe and with an eye on servicing forward-thinking advertising customers, Verve’s solutions are trusted by more than 90 of the United States’ top 100 advertisers, 4,000 publishers globally, and the world’s top demand-side platforms. Learn more at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://verve.com/&quot;&gt;verve.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Verve For Advertisers is a technology company that empowers brands and agencies to target audiences based on declared intent, following them from initial curiosity to ultimate decisioning, to drive measurable outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;ve unified the company&#39;s demand-side offering under the VFA name, bringing together the largest on-site search-intent dataset outside of walled gardens — built on data partnerships with 3M+ websites, LLM chat signals, and survey data — and premium inventory grounded in our direct SDK integrations. Our technology captures both what consumers do and why they do it, delivering high-fidelity audiences, insights, and outcomes across premium omnichannel inventory.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Verve is building a Brand Direct function — a small, senior team that sells and services select brand accounts directly, alongside our existing agency relationships, rather than replacing them. The goal is to get Verve&#39;s data, formats, and capabilities into brand planning conversations earlier, and to prove that dedicated brand-side support grows accounts faster than agency coverage alone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a new team and a founding hire. You&#39;ll help define what “brand direct” looks like at Verve in practice, working closely with the Global VP of Brand Partnerships from day one.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Brand Partnerships Director, UK, you&#39;ll own a portfolio of named brand accounts in the UK, working as a generalist across categories rather than a single vertical. This is a senior individual contributor role — not a people-management role in the first instance — designed for someone who wants to build something and has the option to grow into managing a local team as the function scales.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are a hunter first: someone who can open doors at brand (not agency) level, build credibility fast, and turn a first meeting into a durable, revenue-generating relationship. Prior experience or relationships in a specific vertical (e.g. CPG/Retail, Travel, Finance, Beauty/Lux) are a strong plus, as this role has the potential to grow into leading a vertical specialist team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities include&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build senior brand relationships — Owning relationships at CMO, Global Head of Media, and VP of Brand level, along with key line-of-business leads such as Data, Creative, and Measurement within the brand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Get ahead of the brief — Getting into brand planning cycles early so Verve&#39;s data, formats, and capabilities are already part of the conversation before the brief reaches the agency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Verve in the room — Representing Verve at brand-side (not agency-side) forums, marketing conferences, and roundtables to build Verve&#39;s profile with brand teams directly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commission insight work — Working with the insights and data teams to build brand-specific audience stories, category reports, and trend pieces that give brands a reason to meet and stay engaged.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Secure Joint Business Plans — Working towards annual brand frameworks that lock in investment and strategic commitment at brand level, independent of which agency holds the account.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run the pilot — Building and pitching a defined target list of named accounts, with revenue tracked separately from non-brand-direct-supported business to prove the model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Co-sell, don&#39;t compete — Partner with the existing agency sales team under a joint commercial framework — this role is additive to agency relationships, not competitive with them; revenue is double-counted so both sides are incentivized to collaborate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Here are a few indicators that you&#39;re the right person&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a track record of building and owning senior client relationships directly with brands or marketers, not solely through an agency or intermediary.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have genuine “hunter” instincts — you&#39;re comfortable prospecting, opening new doors, and creating momentum in a newly-created role with no existing playbook.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have an existing network of brand-side contacts in the UK; a specific category or vertical angle (e.g. CPG/Retail, Travel, Finance, Beauty/Lux) is a plus but not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re comfortable with ambiguity and building process as you go — this is a Phase 1 hire into a function that will evolve quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have strong commercial instincts: you can read an account&#39;s growth potential and prioritize your time accordingly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You bring experience in media, adtech, data, or a related commercial sales environment as helpful context, though the core skill this role requires is brand-side relationship building.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Just a few of the benefits waiting for you at Verve:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay healthy with our&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Bupa HealthCare Plan&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;with easy access to medical care&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support your long-term financial security with our&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Aviva Corporate Pension Scheme&lt;/strong&gt;, with Verve contributing 5% of your qualifying earnings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pick what matters most to you in our&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Personalized Benefits Platform,&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;with a budget of&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;£50/month&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recharge with&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;25 paid vacation days + 3 Wellness days&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;throughout the year, in addition to the public holidays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Boost your professional knowledge with our annual training budget &amp;amp; internal webinars&lt;/strong&gt;… and even more reasons to join us!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communications regarding your application will only come from ----- or ----- email addresses.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;Verve provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If you are a California resident subject to the California Consumer Privacy Act, &lt;a href=&quot;https://verve.com/california-applicant-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;click here&lt;/a&gt; to understand how Verve processes your personal information and how you can exercise your rights.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;If you are located in the EU or UK visit our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot; href=&quot;https://verve.com/applicant-privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;privacy policy&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt; to understand how Verve processes your personal information and how you can exercise your rights.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About DevRev&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At DevRev, we&#39;re building the future of work with &lt;em&gt;Computer&lt;/em&gt; – your AI teammate. Unlike traditional tools, &lt;em&gt;Computer&lt;/em&gt; unifies all your data sources, tools, and workflows into a single AI-ready platform, giving employees real-time insights, proactive suggestions, and powerful agentic actions. It extends your existing software with AI-native apps and agents that work alongside your teams and customers – updating workflows, coordinating across teams, and eliminating repetitive work. We call this Team Intelligence: human-AI collaboration that breaks down silos, brings people back together, and frees you to solve bigger problems. Backed by Khosla Ventures and Mayfield with $150M+ raised, DevRev is trusted by global companies across industries.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You own the Arcade Design System - the structural layer every product team at DevRev builds on. You&#39;ll define how components behave across contexts, how tokens translate intent into implementation, and how a growing design team contributes to a coherent system without fragmenting it. This isn&#39;t component art; it&#39;s the architecture that makes an entire platform feel like one mind designed it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own Arcade components end-to-end - from Figma source of truth through token architecture to production, ensuring the gap between spec and shipped product is negligible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and maintain the token system (color, spacing, elevation, typography) - making architectural decisions about naming, hierarchy, and semantic structure that scale across themes and modes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive Figma library governance - versioning, contribution models, and release cadence so product designers always work from a single, trustworthy source.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate directly with engineers on component APIs, prop contracts, and migration paths. You think in implementation terms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn recurring questions into documentation or patterns rather than ad-hoc fixes. Make self-service the default.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;When three teams solve the same problem differently, propose the unified pattern.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor L1-L3 designers on systems thinking through workshops, education sessions, and structured critique.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll bring&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5-8 years of product design experience, with significant time in design systems, component libraries, or platform/infrastructure design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert Figma skills - advanced component architecture, variants, variables, and library management at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design engineering sensibility: comfort with design tokens, CSS custom properties, and component APIs (React or equivalent). You can review a prop contract as naturally as a Figma frame.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of token architecture - not just using tokens but defining hierarchies, naming conventions, and semantic structures that hold across themes, modes, and platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working embedded with engineering on component migration, API design, or design-to-code pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to own outcomes, not outputs - you can point to a migration you drove, an adoption metric you moved, or a systemic problem you resolved permanently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Who you are&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;When you see inconsistency across the product, it&#39;s a structural problem you feel compelled to solve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Before adding a token tier or component variant, you can name every context it will appear in and every team it will affect.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Before finishing any component, you&#39;ve considered its prop contract, token dependencies, Figma structure, and migration path as one coherent decision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You treat the design system as a product and its users as your customers. When a designer is stuck, your instinct is to help them succeed - not to gatekeep correctness. You earn adoption through empathy, responsiveness, and genuine care for the people building on your work. The system&#39;s success is measured by the confidence others feel using it, and that confidence starts with you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You don&#39;t optimize for comfort - you optimize for the platform, even when that means reworking your own earlier decisions as the system evolves.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
