&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are a global team of innovators and pioneers dedicated to shaping the future of observability. At New Relic, we build an intelligent platform that empowers companies to thrive in an AI-first world by giving them unparalleled insight into their complex systems. As we continue to expand our global footprint, we&#39;re looking for passionate people to join our mission. If you&#39;re ready to help the world&#39;s best companies optimize their digital applications, we invite you to explore a career with us!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;19&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;19&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Senior Legal Counsel, EMEA&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;20&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;20&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Your opportunity&lt;/strong&gt; We are looking for a Senior Legal Counsel (EMEA) based in the UK with deep SaaS commercial transaction experience to join our collaborative, forward-thinking legal team. Whether you are ready to take a decisive step up into a senior role or an established Senior Counsel seeking broader scope and higher-impact challenges, this role offers the platform to drive your career forward.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;21&quot;&gt;At New Relic, legal isn’t just a support function: you will sit directly at the deal table, driving revenue growth, optimising customer and partner relationships, and scaling our SaaS business across the EMEA region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;22&quot;&gt;You will enjoy direct visibility, genuine autonomy, and the space to shape your own career trajectory within a globally dispersed team. If you thrive in a dynamic environment, enjoy solving complex commercial challenges, and want to directly power our go-to-market strategy, this is the role for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;23&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;23&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-path-to-node=&quot;24&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;24,0,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;24,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Structure &amp;amp; Close SaaS Deals:&lt;/strong&gt; Draft, review, and negotiate complex SaaS agreements, including data processing addenda and security terms in direct support of EMEA go-to-market efforts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;24,1,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;24,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Empower Sales Teams:&lt;/strong&gt; Coach and advise regional sales teams on SaaS deal structure, negotiation tactics, and customer dispute resolution to accelerate sales velocity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;24,2,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;24,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Scale Channel Partnerships:&lt;/strong&gt; Work closely with Partner business teams to structure, negotiate, and expand business via resellers, MSPs, distributors, and global system integrators.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;24,3,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;24,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Lead Privacy &amp;amp; Regulatory Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Collaborate with Privacy Legal to embed practical risk-tolerance strategies and standardise commercial contract responses under global privacy regimes (GDPR, DORA, etc.).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;24,4,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;24,4,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Build Scalable Infrastructure:&lt;/strong&gt; Own, refine, and modernise SaaS agreement templates, negotiation playbooks, and contract escalation workflows to ensure legal scales alongside business growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;24,5,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;24,5,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Serve as a Trusted Advisor:&lt;/strong&gt; Provide pragmatic, risk-aware legal guidance across cross-functional partners, including Marketing, Product, Finance, and Contract Managers, aligning legal strategy with our consumption-based model, monetisation, and product-led growth (PLG) goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;25&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;25&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;This role requires&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-path-to-node=&quot;26&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;26,0,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;26,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Mandatory SaaS Commercial Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Substantial experience drafting and negotiating complex SaaS commercial contracts, partner frameworks, and cloud technology agreements with a solid knowledge of revenue recognition principles.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;26,1,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;26,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Educational &amp;amp; Qualification Background (UK):&lt;/strong&gt; Qualified to practice law and in good standing with the relevant professional regulatory body (e.g., state bar, Solicitors Regulation Authority, or equivalent) in your jurisdiction of residence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;26,2,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;26,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Privacy &amp;amp; Security Fluency:&lt;/strong&gt; Solid hands-on knowledge of data privacy, artificial intelligence, security topics, and global compliance frameworks within commercial SaaS transactions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;26,3,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;26,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;GTM &amp;amp; Sales Alignment:&lt;/strong&gt; Proactive, strategic approach to working directly alongside enterprise sales teams to drive deal execution across the EMEA region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;26,4,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;26,4,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Autonomy &amp;amp; Resilience:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven ability to manage competing deliverables, set clear boundaries, prioritise under deadlines, and operate independently in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;26,5,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;26,5,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Collaborative Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Outstanding interpersonal skills with a track record of building trust across functions, regions, and executive levels.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;27&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;27&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Bonus points if you have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-path-to-node=&quot;28&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;28,0,0&quot;&gt;In-house legal experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;28,1,0&quot;&gt;Familiarity with consumption-based pricing models in SaaS.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;28,2,0&quot;&gt;Direct experience handling GSI/Reseller partner agreements and advising marketing teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;28,3,0&quot;&gt;An eagerness to leverage AI, with a deep understanding of AI products, LLMs, and the product lifecycle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;28,4,0&quot;&gt;Privacy certifications (e.g., CIPP/E) or deep familiarity with the EU AI Act and DORA.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;29&quot;&gt;#LI-Remote #LI-JJ2&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Fostering a diverse, welcoming and inclusive environment is important to us. We work hard to make everyone feel comfortable bringing their best, most authentic selves to work every day. We celebrate our talented Relics’ different backgrounds and abilities, and recognize the different paths they took to reach us – including nontraditional ones. Their experiences and perspectives inspire us to make our products and company the best they can be. We’re looking for people who feel connected to our mission and values, not just candidates who check off all the boxes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete any part of the application or recruiting process, please reach out to &lt;a ----- -----
&lt;p&gt;We believe in empowering all Relics to achieve professional and business success through a flexible workforce model. This model allows us to work in a variety of workplaces that best support our success, including fully office-based, fully remote, or hybrid.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our hiring process&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;In compliance with applicable law, all persons hired will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work and to complete employment eligibility verification. Note: Our stewardship of the data of thousands of customers means that a criminal background check is required to join New Relic.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We will consider qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records based on individual circumstances and in accordance with applicable law including, but not limited to, the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://sfgov.org/olse/sites/default/files/FCO%20poster2020.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Headhunters and recruitment agencies may not submit resumes/CVs through this website or directly to managers. New Relic does not accept unsolicited headhunter and agency resumes, and will not pay fees to any third-party agency or company that does not have a signed agreement with New Relic.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;New Relic develops and distributes encryption software and technology that complies with U.S. export controls and licensing requirements. Certain New Relic roles require candidates to pass an export compliance assessment as a condition of employment in any global location. If relevant, we will provide more information later in the application process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Candidates are evaluated based on qualifications, regardless of race, religion, ethnicity, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender expression or identity, age, disability, neurodiversity, veteran or marital status, political viewpoint, or other legally protected characteristics.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Review our Applicant Privacy Notice at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://newrelic.com/termsandconditions/applicant-privacy-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;https://newrelic.com/termsandconditions/applicant-privacy-policy&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-family: &#39;Instrument Sans&#39;, &#39;Segoe UI&#39;, Trebuchet MS, Tahoma, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Vast is developing next-generation &lt;strong&gt;space stations and space infrastructure&lt;/strong&gt; using an incremental, hardware-rich, and low-cost approach. Vast is rapidly developing its multi-module Haven Station to ensure a continuous human presence in space for America and its allies, enabling advanced microgravity research and manufacturing, and unlocking a new space economy for government, corporate, and private customers. Haven Demo’s 2025 success made Vast the only operational commercial space station company to fly and operate its own spacecraft. Next, Haven-1 is expected to become the world’s first commercial space station when it launches in 2027, followed by additional Haven modules. Additionally, the company recently announced &lt;strong&gt;Vast Satellite&lt;/strong&gt;, a high-power satellite product line leveraging its space station components and the heritage of Haven Demo.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Headquartered in&lt;strong&gt; Long Beach, California&lt;/strong&gt;, and with more than 1,000 employees and over a billion dollars in private capital, Vast has built the facilities required to manufacture and operate America’s next space station. The company plans to develop future habitats and systems for the Moon and Mars, dedicated space stations for government partners, and other crewed systems that will unlock the expanding long-term space economy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Vast recherche un(e) &lt;strong&gt;Directeur(trice), Développement Commercial International - Satellites&lt;/strong&gt;, sous la responsabilité du &lt;strong&gt;SVP, Satellite Business Development &amp;amp; Commercialization&lt;/strong&gt;, pour diriger le développement commercial axé sur le commerce (communications, observation de la Terre, détection, défense et applications de calcul en orbite) et les gouvernements internationaux pour Vast Satellites. Ce rôle est centré sur les marchés hors États-Unis — notamment l&#39;Europe, le Moyen-Orient et l&#39;Asie — et dirigera l&#39;engagement client, le développement des opportunités, la stratégie de capture, l&#39;engagement gouvernemental/défense et les efforts de partenariat qui font progresser les initiatives de Vast pour développer, fabriquer et exploiter des plateformes de bus satellites avancées.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Il s&#39;agit d&#39;une petite équipe commerciale fondatrice de haut niveau : le rôle exige à la fois des instincts de « hunter » en développement commercial (créer des marchés et de la demande là où il n&#39;en existe pas encore) et des compétences avérées de « closer » (négocier et exécuter des contrats allant de quelques millions à des centaines de millions de dollars).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ce poste sera à &lt;strong&gt;temps plein, exempté&lt;/strong&gt;, ouvert à un lieu de travail international flexible comme décrit ci-dessus.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsabilités :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Élaborer et exécuter une stratégie globale de marché commercial et gouvernemental international couvrant l&#39;Europe, le Moyen-Orient et l&#39;Asie, alignée sur les objectifs commerciaux de Vast.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Établir et maintenir une veille stratégique sur le marché et la concurrence concernant les clients spatiaux commerciaux et gouvernementaux internationaux, en distinguant le positionnement de Vast de celui de ses concurrents dans chaque région.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Piloter la planification interne pour la priorisation des opportunités internationales, la stratégie de capture et le développement du pipeline sur de multiples marchés alliés et partenaires.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diriger l&#39;engagement client à travers l&#39;identification d&#39;opportunités, la définition du périmètre des missions, les présentations de capacités et le développement de concepts précoces avec les opérateurs commerciaux internationaux, les sociétés d&#39;observation de la Terre, les ministères de la défense et les entités gouvernementales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tirer parti d&#39;un solide réseau préexistant de haut niveau au sein de la chaîne de valeur internationale de l&#39;espace et de la défense pour ouvrir des portes auprès de clients potentiels et identifier précocement les menaces concurrentielles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diriger l&#39;élaboration des propositions et coordonner les contributions interfonctionnelles des équipes d&#39;ingénierie, de gestion de programme, de finance, juridique et de contrôle des exportations/conformité, avec le soutien de l&#39;analyste BD et de l&#39;ingénieur avant-vente de l&#39;équipe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assumer la responsabilité du développement du pipeline, des prévisions et des rapports pour tous les comptes commerciaux et gouvernementaux internationaux.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Négocier et conclure des contrats pour des missions commerciales et gouvernementales/défense internationales et les services associés, en naviguant à travers divers cadres nationaux de passation de marchés, de contrôle des exportations (ex. ITAR/EAR) et de partenariat.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Se coordonner avec l&#39;équipe de sécurité nationale de Vast lorsque les programmes internationaux croisent des parties prenantes ou des enjeux liés au gouvernement américain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Représenter Vast lors d&#39;événements de l&#39;industrie spatiale, aérospatiale et de défense internationale en Europe, au Moyen-Orient et en Asie.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Faire des présentations, participer à des panels et fournir des briefings de haut niveau/C-suite communiquant les capacités et la valeur des plateformes satellites de Vast aux audiences commerciales, gouvernementales et de défense internationales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications Minimales :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plus de 12 ans d&#39;expérience pertinente dans le développement commercial spatial/aérospatial, les ventes, la gestion de capture ou les contrats gouvernementaux/défense, avec un succès avéré en Europe, au Moyen-Orient et/ou en Asie.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Historique avéré d&#39;origination et de conclusion personnelle de contrats, y compris des transactions de plusieurs dizaines de millions de dollars ou plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relations établies et vérifiables avec des clients potentiels au niveau cadre et exécutif, et connaissance du paysage concurrentiel sur de multiples marchés spatiaux et de défense internationaux.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expérience dans la chaîne de valeur spatiale/aérospatiale (lancement, bus satellite, charge utile, intégration maître d&#39;œuvre ou opérations), idéalement complémentaire des opérations satellites — par ex. observation de la Terre ou défense internationale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compréhension approfondie des structures de passation de marchés et de partenariat gouvernementales internationales pertinentes pour les programmes d&#39;espace et de défense.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solides compétences techniques et capacité à communiquer des systèmes complexes à des audiences commerciales, de défense et gouvernementales internationales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellentes capacités de communication, d&#39;analyse, de collaboration et de relations interpersonnelles ; à l&#39;aise pour opérer à travers diverses cultures et langues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capacité à opérer de manière autonome, à hiérarchiser les priorités efficacement et à gérer simultanément plusieurs projets internationaux dans un environnement de petite équipe au rythme soutenu.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compétences et Expériences Souhaitées :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relations et crédibilité établies en Europe, au Moyen-Orient et en Asie.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maîtrise des langues pertinentes pour les marchés cibles (français, arabe, japonais, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expérience de travail aux côtés d&#39;équipes d&#39;affaires publiques locales ou coordination avec celles-ci (ex. affaires publiques gouvernementales françaises/UE).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connaissance des régimes de contrôle des exportations (ITAR/EAR) dans les programmes de satellites internationaux.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Exigences Supplémentaires :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capacité à voyager plus de 50 % du temps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Vast is looking for a&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Director, Satellite Business Development International&lt;/strong&gt;, reporting to the &lt;strong&gt;SVP, Satellite Business Development &amp;amp; Commercialization&lt;/strong&gt;, to lead commercial (communications, Earth observation, sensing, defense, and in-orbit compute applications) and international government-focused business development for Vast Satellites. This role is focused on markets outside the United States — including Europe, the Middle East, and Asia — and will lead customer engagement, opportunity development, capture strategy, government/defense engagement, and partnership efforts that advance Vast&#39;s initiatives to develop, manufacture, and operate advanced satellite bus platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a small, senior founding commercial team: the role demands both business development &quot;hunter&quot; instincts (creating markets and demand where none exist yet) and proven &quot;closer&quot; skills (negotiating and executing contracts from single-digit millions to hundreds of millions of dollars).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This will be a &lt;strong&gt;full-time, exempt&lt;/strong&gt; position open to a flexible international location as described above.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute a comprehensive international commercial and government market strategy spanning Europe, the Middle East, and Asia, aligned with Vast&#39;s business objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain a market and competitive intelligence view across international commercial and government space customers, distinguishing Vast&#39;s positioning from competitors in each region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead internal planning for international opportunity prioritization, capture strategy, and pipeline development across multiple allied and partner markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead customer engagement across opportunity identification, mission scoping, capability briefings, and early concept development with international commercial operators, Earth observation companies, defense ministries, and government entities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage a strong, pre-existing senior-level network across the international space/defense value chain to open doors with potential customers and identify competitive threats early.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead proposal development and coordinate cross-functional contributions from engineering, program management, finance, legal, and export-control/compliance teams, supported by the team&#39;s BD analyst and pre-sales engineer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own pipeline development, forecasting, and reporting across all international commercial and government accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiate and close contracts for international commercial and government/defense missions and associated services, navigating varying national procurement, export-control (e.g., ITAR/EAR), and partnership frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with Vast&#39;s National Security team where international programs intersect with US Government stakeholders or content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Vast at international space, aerospace, and defense industry events across Europe, the Middle East, and Asia.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver presentations, participate in panels, and provide senior/C-suite-level briefings that communicate the capabilities and value of Vast&#39;s satellite platforms to international commercial, government, and defense audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of relevant experience in space/aerospace business development, sales, capture management, or government/defense contracting, with demonstrated success operating in Europe, the Middle East, and/or Asia.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of personally originating and closing contracts, including deals in the tens of millions of dollars or above.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established, verifiable senior and executive-level relationships with potential customers, and knowledge of the competitive landscape across multiple international space/defense markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in the space/aerospace value chain (launch, satellite bus, payload, prime integration, or operations), ideally complementary to satellite operations — e.g., Earth observation or international defense.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of international government procurement and partnership structures relevant to space and defense programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical understanding and ability to communicate complex systems to international commercial, defense, and government audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, analytical, collaboration, and interpersonal skills; comfortable operating across cultures and languages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate independently, prioritize effectively, and manage multiple international efforts simultaneously in a fast-paced, lean-team environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Skills &amp;amp; Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Existing relationships and credibility across Europe, the Middle East, and Asia.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in languages relevant to target markets (French, Arabic, Japanese, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working alongside or coordinating with in-country government affairs teams (e.g., French/EU government affairs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with export-control regimes (ITAR/EAR) in international satellite programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel 50%+ of the time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-family: &#39;Instrument Sans&#39;, &#39;Segoe UI&#39;, Trebuchet MS, Tahoma, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1; font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;We calibrate level and compensation to the selected candidate&#39;s experience and demonstrated capability. We welcome applicants across a range of experience levels to apply.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Base salary will vary depending on job-related knowledge, education, skills, experience, business needs, and market demand. Salary is just one component of our comprehensive compensation package. Full-time employees also receive company equity, as well as access to a full suite of compelling benefits and perks, including: medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and dependents, generous paid time off; up to 20+ days of vacation for exempt staff and up to 10+ days of vacation for non-exempt staff with the ability to cash-out unused vacation annually, paid parental leave, short and long-term disability insurance, life insurance, access to a 401(k) retirement plan, ClassPass credits, personalized mental healthcare through Spring Health, and other discounts and perks. We also take pride in offering exceptional food perks, with snacks, drip coffee &amp;amp; onsite barista, cold drinks, and dinner meals remaining free of charge, and lunch subsidized as part of Vast’s ongoing commitment to providing high-quality meals for employees.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;U.S. EXPORT CONTROL COMPLIANCE STATUS&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;The person hired will have access to information and items subject to U.S. export controls, and therefore, must either be a “U.S. person” as defined by&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-22/section-120.62&quot;&gt;22 C.F.R. § 120.62&lt;/a&gt; or otherwise eligible for deemed export licensing. This status includes U.S. citizens, U.S. nationals, lawful permanent residents (green card holders), and asylees and refugees with such status granted, not pending.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EQUAL OPPORTUNITY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Vast is an Equal Opportunity Employer; employment with Vast is governed on the basis of merit, competence and qualifications and will not be influenced in any manner by race, color, religion, gender, national origin/ethnicity, veteran status, disability status, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, marital status, mental or physical disability or any other legally protected status.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;As an Enterprise Customer Success Manager, you will proactively drive new product attachment and effective strong relationships across our largest and most strategic customers. You’ll advocate for the customer internally and focus on a positive customer experience. Interactions are rooted in relationship-management, first and foremost, while also advocating for growth opportunities. Enterprise Customer Success Managers follow a well-defined methodology that helps them identify the customer&#39;s unique needs and clearly convey the value of the Datadog product.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Datadog, we place value in our office culture - the relationships and collaboration it builds and the creativity it brings to the table. We operate as a hybrid workplace to ensure our Datadogs can create a work-life harmony that best fits them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a strategic partner to customers, orchestrating cross-functional internal teams and engaging executive, technical, and business stakeholders to understand customer goals and translate them into a clear, deliverable Datadog value narrative.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively build and maintain executive relationships to deliver clear, outcome-driven value stories that connect Datadog technical use cases to measurable business results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead QBRs and strategic reviews as a forum to demonstrate impact, align on priorities, and define next-step initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze adoption and usage trends to quantify value delivered, extract insights from large datasets, identify gaps, and drive financially grounded commercial recommendations and strategic opportunities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Position Datadog as a critical observability platform that enables reliability, efficiency, and informed decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and project manage the on-boarding process for new customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally with AEs, SEs, TAM, Product, Support, Enablement and other technical teams to ensure consistent value delivery and messaging.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;With demonstrated understanding of observability and security platforms, align customers technical and business objectives to our platform offerings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer-centric with 3+ years in a Customer Success or Account Management role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to manage a wide portfolio of accounts rolling up to large enterprise corporate accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledgeable in working with Fortune 1000 companies and global brands across all industries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong communicator with exceptional attention to detail and an ability to cater to a specific audience, including CTO, VP of Engineering and DevOps professionals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced in the B2B tech space or with SaaS companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to travel for customer onsite visits and events as required&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in written and spoken English and German&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Datadog values people from all walks of life. We understand not everyone will meet all the above qualifications on day one. That&#39;s okay. If you’re passionate about technology and want to grow your skills, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits and Growth:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Best-in-breed onboarding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous global benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intra-departmental mentor and buddy program for in-house networking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;New hire stock equity (RSUs) and employee stock purchase plan (ESPP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuous professional development, product training, and career pathing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An inclusive company culture, able to join our Community Guilds and Inclusion Talks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Benefits and Growth listed above may vary based on the country of your employment and the nature of your employment with Datadog.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Datadog:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Datadog is the leading observability and security platform for the AI era, providing businesses with unified visibility across the technology stack to manage complexity at scale. It brings applications, infrastructure, data, models, and security into one place, using AI to detect and resolve issues before they impact customers. Trusted globally by Fortune 500 companies and high-growth AI leaders, Datadog enables businesses to move faster with clarity and confidence. Learn more about #DatadogLife on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/datadoghq/?hl=en&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Instagram&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/datadog&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;LinkedIn,&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://learn.datadoghq.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Datadog Learning Center. &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;215&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Equal Opportunity at Datadog:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Datadog is proud to offer &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eeoc.gov/sites/default/files/2023-06/22-088_EEOC_KnowYourRights6.12ScreenRdr.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;equal employment opportunity&lt;/a&gt; to everyone regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity, veteran status, and other characteristics protected by law. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements. Here are our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.datadoghq.com/legal/candidate-legal-notices/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Legal Notices&lt;/a&gt; for your reference.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Datadog endeavors to make our Careers Page accessible to all users. If you would like to contact us regarding the accessibility of our website or need assistance completing the application process, please complete &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeoJeduEZ2NdZF_65uZmWUrCM-zee7yADXX1s6Xr9zAGq8iKA/viewform&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;this form&lt;/a&gt;. This form is for accommodation requests only and cannot be used to inquire about the status of applications.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;662&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Privacy and AI Guidelines:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;662&quot;&gt;Any information you submit to Datadog as part of your application will be processed in accordance with Datadog’s&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.datadoghq.com/legal/applicant-candidate-privacy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.datadoghq.com/legal/applicant-candidate-privacy/&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;Applicant and Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;. For information on our AI policy, please visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.datadoghq.com/legal/interviewing-at-datadog-ai-guidelines/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Interviewing at Datadog AI Guidelines&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Global Structure&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;Deliveroo is now part of DoorDash, bringing together teams with even greater reach, scale, and ambition. Depending on your role, you may collaborate with teammates, systems, and leaders across DoorDash and Wolt. Together, we’re unlocking new possibilities as one global team.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Rejoignez-nous dans notre mission de transformer la façon dont le monde mange et fait ses courses. Chez Deliveroo, impact, innovation et croissance sont au cœur de tout ce que nous faisons. Nous connectons les consommateurs, les restaurants, les magasins et les livreurs partenaires pour donner à chaque personne la possibilité d&#39;acheter ce qu&#39;elle veut, comme elle le veut, quand elle le veut et où elle le veut.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Nous sommes une entreprise axée sur la technologie, à l&#39;avant-garde d’un secteur qui connaît une des expansions les plus rapides au monde. Nous avançons rapidement, valorisons l&#39;autonomie, et sommes toujours en recherche de nouvelles idées et de personnes talentueuses pour nous rejoindre!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ce que vous ferez au quotidien&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;En tant que &lt;strong&gt;Account Associate - Retail &amp;amp; Grocery (H/F)&lt;/strong&gt;, vous serez responsable du succès d’un portefeuille de partenaires, afin d’assurer la meilleure expérience à nos utilisateurs, tout en construisant un partenariat solide et durable avec nos eux pour notre application.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Analysez la performance de votre portefeuille et prenez les mesures adéquates, faites des recommandations, soyez agile et ouvert à la nouveauté.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Optimisation et gestion de Processus : Deliveroo est une société qui évolue à grande vitesse et à grande échelle. Vous aurez l’opportunité de créer et améliorer des processus, par exemple la gestion de partenariats pour contribuer à la croissance. Vous élaborerez des documents de meilleures pratiques pour des comptes spécifiques et pour l&#39;ensemble du portefeuille&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Relations avec les magasins Retail et/ou Grocery : Vous gérerez le développement des partenariats, le suivi des données, et vous assurerez une expérience optimale sur l’application afin de faire de Deliveroo le service de livraison à domicile de référence, en apportant votre expertise Food Tech en étant l&#39;expert de votre zone / ville.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Vous veillerez au suivi du respect des engagements contractuels pris avec les partenaires de votre portefeuille.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ce qu’il vous faut pour réussir&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Expérience : stage ou alternance dans un rôle d’Account management ou commercial. Une expérience terrain au sein d’un grand groupe (idéalement supermarché, marketplace, ecommerce, retailer, FMCG) est un vrai atout.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Commercial : vous avez à cœur de négocier, d’anticiper des discussions commerciales, d’entreprendre des actions afin de maintenir un portefeuille de qualité (discussions contractuelles, négociations de mise en place d&#39;outils commerciaux, etc)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Entrepreneur : vous avez le goût pour entreprendre, créer, aller chercher des opportunités, en sachant prendre de la hauteur mais sans jamais se couper du terrain et de votre téléphone pour comprendre vos partenaires.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Analytique :  capable d’être synthétique, d&#39;approfondir les données et de comprendre les données qui permettent d&#39;améliorer les performances pour nos partenaires en magasins.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Proactif(-ive) dans vos relations avec les interlocuteurs. Vous adorez être sur le terrain et vous êtes impliqué(e) dans tout ce qui est opérationnel dans votre périmètre.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Centré sur le client : être obsédé par nos clients. Utiliser des données quantitatives et qualitatives pour construire un service qui soit opérationnellement excellent pour nos clients.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Jouer en équipe : un joueur d&#39;équipe qui collabore et qui est capable de tirer le meilleur parti des personnes qui vous entourent. Capable de travailler efficacement à tous les niveaux de Deliveroo et de réussir avec et par les autres.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Optimiste, confiant et plein d&#39;énergie :  vous apportez de la fraîcheur, de l&#39;énergie et de la passion dans l&#39;équipe.  Vous contribuez à créer un environnement de travail unique, propice aux nouvelles idées et agréable pour les autres personnes impliquées.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Langues : Français et Anglais courant indispensables. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pourquoi nous rejoindre ?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Nous sommes des passionnés de food, des problem-solvers, des créateurs de communauté et bien plus encore. Ce qui nous rassemble : un esprit entrepreneurial fort et l’envie de construire quelque chose d’ambitieux ensemble.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;🔧 Une grande autonomie pour avoir un impact concret sur votre portefeuille et nos partenaires.&lt;br&gt;🌱 Un environnement stimulant favorisant l’apprentissage, le développement et l’évolution de carrière.&lt;br&gt;💙 Des avantages pensés pour le bien-être et l’équilibre de nos équipes.&lt;br&gt;🌍 Une culture inclusive, internationale et collaborative où chacun peut trouver sa place.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;À compétences égales, ce poste est ouvert aux travailleurs et travailleuses en situation de handicap ou assimilés au sens de l’article L5212-13 du Code du travail. Deliveroo s’engage en faveur de la diversité, l’égalité professionnelle, l’emploi des personnes en situation de handicap.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Prêt(e) à contribuer au futur de la foodtech ? Postulez dès aujourd’hui !&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Diversity, Equity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;At Deliveroo, we know that a great workplace reflects the world around us and that true diversity and inclusion make us stronger, more creative, and better at what we do. We’re committed to fostering an environment where everyone can do their best work and feel they belong.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe in equality of opportunity and welcome candidates from all backgrounds regardless of age, gender, ethnicity, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, socio-economic background, religion, or belief.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you have a disability or long-term health condition and need support to apply for one of our roles, or require any reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process, you’ll have the opportunity to let us know once you’ve submitted your application. We’ll share details on how to request support so we can ensure you have a fair and equitable experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re excited about making a real impact in a fast-moving marketplace and growing your career alongside ambitious, supportive teams, we’d love to hear from you!&lt;/p&gt;
